    "proof": "The normalized even Legendre polynomials form an orthonormal sequence, hence f_n converges weakly to zero. A compact operator maps every bounded weakly null sequence to a norm-null sequence: otherwise a norm-convergent subsequence of Kf_n would have a nonzero limit, while all its scalar products converge to zero. Therefore |<Kf_n,f_n>|<=||Kf_n|| tends to zero. TICKET-248 gives Q0(f_n)<=11/n. Substitution into a proposed positive coercive inequality gives c<=0, a contradiction. The finite-rank projection rows are exact checks of the compact mechanism, not the proof for arbitrary compact K.",
